  "description": "The section 1.5 records are written day by day and what remains is read at the end of each row's day: nothing on 2 June; Story 1 awaiting review on 16 June (begin act citing record 2); on 17 June E-lacquer's finish, outstanding, nested under Story 1, which the directive ended (Story 1's end act and E-lacquer's begin act both cite record 5); nothing on 20 June, when record 6 fulfils E-lacquer and its end act cites it; and, once the application records the 20 June revision as Story 2, that story. Every row reads the same again with all records present.",
  "note": "7.6.7: \"An expectation property whose first period is nested under exactly one story (7.6.15), because a review of that story began it, is part of that story, its middle: its begin and end acts, and the revisions of them (7.6.10), are Assertions on that story Item in the same form, `(story, <event context>, story)`.\" The act names follow README section 7, Story-held expectation property acts: `(<story>, \"<story>/exp:<path>/b<n>\", <story>)`, with `/e<n>` and `/v<n>` likewise.",
